  "_frames": "index = m | q<<1 | z<<2 : 0 m0q0z0, 1 m1q0z0, 2 m0q1z0, 3 m1q1z0, 4 m0q0z1, 5 m1q0z1, 6 m0q1z1, 7 m1q1z1",
  "_axes": "Morph raises every Fc by a fifth. Freq. Tracking narrows the six parametric poles. Transform 2 lifts sections 4-7 an octave and +4 dB, and opens the low pass section an octave.",
  "_sections": "S1 is E-MU's Low Pass Section: pole at Fc, zero at 2.5 kHz so the fall stops and the section is a shelf, not an endless rolloff. Talking Hedz opposes its ends the same way — its S1 rises and its S6 falls, which is why the total sits at 0 dB. S2-S7 are Parametric Equalizer Sections: pole and zero at the same Fc, pole ten times tighter, so each is a boost over unity rather than a bandpass.",
